*.jpg
# Video, for the same reason as the lines above it. The capture fixtures are
# real footage of real people; their photographs and their voices are already
# kept out of the repository and their video belongs on the same side of that
# line. Git history does not forget, so this is not something to fix later.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm
.huggingface/
.gitnexus

# Redis dev snapshot — a local artifact, never a source file
dump.rdb

# Deploy secrets and built portal output.
#
# deploy/staging/.env and app.env ARE tracked, deliberately, and hold FRESHLY
# GENERATED values that have never protected any real data — so a clone is
# deployable without a scavenger hunt. They are not the secrets of any live
# deployment, and a real one's values must never be committed over them:
# MEDIA_KEK is not recoverable and a leaked one decrypts every sealed media
# blob. Regenerate with deploy/gen-secrets.sh; keep real values out of band.
#
# prod.env stays ignored with no exception — production secrets protect real
# subjects' media and have no business in version control at any point.
deploy/prod.env
deploy/.env
deploy/www/
# Negations, and they must come AFTER the broad `.env*` rule further up or that
# rule wins — git applies the last matching pattern, not the most specific.
!deploy/staging/.env
!deploy/staging/app.env

# Supabase CLI local scratch state. .temp/start-secrets holds the CLI's
# well-known local demo keys and a generated DB password — worthless off this
# machine, but a secret-shaped file in git history is a liability regardless, and
# .branches is per-developer state that conflicts on every merge.
backend/supabase/.temp/
backend/supabase/.branches/
